    Bug 2028076 - Allow additional properties for annotated schema files. r=vineet

    The `Settings` type is referencing `get()`, `set()` and `clear()` functions:
    https://searchfox.org/comm-central/rev/43722a27c71ed75d0d50bfd680f0476e61f6a9c1/mozilla/toolkit/components/extensions/schemas/types.json#29-136

    The WebExtension schema format does not support a property which identifies if a
    setting is defined as read-only, this is currently a pure implementation detail:
    https://searchfox.org/comm-central/source/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-messengerSettings.js#59

    We do not want to document `set()` and `clear()` functions for read-only settings.
    This is solved by adding an `additional_properties` entry to the annotation data,
    which is merged into the annotated schema files and then processed by the automated
    WebExtension documentation generator.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D291151

diff --git a/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md b/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md
index b2de65025a2..13accb9f994 100644
--- a/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md
+++ b/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md
@@ -29,6 +29,14 @@ the provided annotation should be added to the browser_compat_data [3] repositor
 The annotation files can also provide `enums` objects with `annotations` arrays
 for the supported enum values.

+Annotation objects can also be `additional_properties` objects, which provide
+additional structured metadata which may be used for the documentation. The
+following additional properties are supported:
+
+- `readOnly` - a boolean value (`true`) on a `types.Setting` property, indicating
+that this setting is read-only. Read-only settings will only document the `get()`
+method, the `set()` and `clear()` methods will be omitted.
+
 The annotation information is used by the webext-schema-generator [1], which is
 providing a post-processed set of authoritative schema files for the Thunderbird
 project at [2]. These files can be used as the single source of truth for the
